Even with the smiley there, this could cause immense
confusion.

It's hard to remember just how long NetHack has been
around compared to other stuff.

The NPL isn't the GPL because there was a race
condition, it was written the same year the GPL was
written [and may well predate the GPL].

Instead, the _document on which the NPL is based_
_predates_ the original GPL by a year.

Here's the GNU licence copyright notice:

    GNU GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE

    Copyright (C) 1989, 1991 Free Software
    Foundation, Inc.
    51 Franklin Street, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA
    02110-1301, USA

    http://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl.html

However, the NPL _is_ based on the BISON general
public license, Richard Stallman's earlier cut at
what became the GPL, so it is surely compatible in
"ideals" with that later GPL license.

Here's the NPL copyright notice"

           NETHACK GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE
           (Copyright 1989 M. Stephenson)

    (Based on the BISON general public license,
        copyright 1988 Richard M. Stallman)

    [Found in http://www.nethack.org somewhere, and
    embedded in every download of NetHack]

